# secli host launcher configuration example.
#
# Copy this file to config/secli.conf and uncomment the keys you want to
# change. The configuration file applies to the git clone deployment; the
# Nix package deployment is configured through environment variables.
# See docs/config.md for the full reference.
#
# Format rules:
#   - one SECLI_KEY=value assignment per line
#   - empty lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored
#   - unknown keys are rejected
#   - later assignments override earlier ones
#
# Precedence: environment variable > configuration file > built-in default.

# Project directory whitelist, colon-separated absolute paths.
# Default: /data/projects
# Example adding a scratch directory:
#SECLI_ALLOWED_PROJECT_PREFIXES=/data/projects:/tmp

# Full image reference used by the host launcher.
# Default: ghcr.io/hinnyuu/secli:<VERSION>, where <VERSION> is read from
# the VERSION file in the deployment root.
#SECLI_IMAGE=localhost/secli:dev

# State root holding the per-CLI Homes.
# Default: <deployment root>/state
#SECLI_STATE_DIR=/secure/path/secli-state
